# Keep the service image build context small: only service/ is COPY'd.
# Without this, docker build -f service/Dockerfile . transfers .venv,
# dist/ and .git as well, plus local databases and scratch data.
.git
.venv
.venv-fuzz
dist
build
.gitignore
.github
Makefile
MANIFEST.in
pyproject.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.gitattributes
# Test and profile caches hold generated, non-source data and differ per
# host; `__pycache__` needs the `**/` form, because a bare pattern only
# matches at the context root and the package's own `__pycache__` (and
# `.hypothesis`) would otherwise be sent in the context. They are never
# COPY'd, but they bloat the transfer and invalidate the layer cache on
# every local run.
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
**.hypothesis
.scratch
docs
tests
fuzzers
benchmarks
# Local databases and benchmark data are sensitive corpus data and are
# never COPY'd into the service image; keep them out of the context too.
# `*.db` and `*.sqlite3` as written only match at the context root, so
# the `**/` forms cover a database generated under a package or data
# directory instead of next to the Dockerfile's call site. The -wal/-shm
# sidecars carry the same corpus data as the database they belong to, so
# they get the same nested forms.
*.db
**.db
*.db-wal
**.db-wal
*.db-shm
**.db-shm
*.sqlite3
**.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
**.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
**.sqlite3-shm
data
scale_data
# Go test and fuzz files are never compiled into the service binary;
# excluding them keeps test-only edits from invalidating the image layer
# and keeps test dependencies out of the build context. The patterns
# use wildcards over the Go tree's known package depths, not one entry
# per file, so a newly added test file is excluded by default instead
# of silently re-entering the context until someone notices it here.
service/*_test.go
service/cmd/*/*_test.go
service/internal/*/*_test.go
